            <ArticleTitle>Cardiovascular complications on upper vagal rootlet section for glossopharyngeal neuralgia; case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>248-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute hypotension and right bundle-branch block occurred when the authors sectioned the uppermost rootlet of the vagus nerve in a case of glossopharyngeal neuralgia. Hypotension lasted for 20 minutes and arrhythmia for 4 days. A possible mechanism is discussed and cardiovascular disorders are reviewed in similar cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
